    "lines": [
      {
        "text": "A floor plan, drawn in pencil. With them in it."
      },
      {
        "text": "Nadia tracked down the previous owner's daughter, Mrs. Albrecht.",
        "say": "Nadia tracked down the previous owner's daughter, Mrs. /ˈɑlbɹɛkt/.",
        "pauseBefore": 0.4
      },
      {
        "text": "There's a room behind our hallway wall.",
        "speaker": "nadia",
        "pauseBefore": 0.5
      },
      {
        "text": "Father bricked up that room in 1974.",
        "say": "Father bricked up that room in nineteen-seventy-four.",
        "speaker": "albrecht",
        "pauseBefore": 0.5
      },
      {
        "text": "He said it was for the tenant.",
        "speaker": "albrecht",
        "pauseBefore": 0.45
      },
      {
        "text": "There was never a tenant. Not on any lease.",
        "pauseBefore": 0.45
      },
      {
        "text": "That night, Nadia measured the gap again. Ninety-one centimeters.",
        "pauseBefore": 0.45
      },
      {
        "text": "The next night, ninety-two.",
        "pauseBefore": 0.45
      },
      {
        "text": "Then ninety-three.",
        "pauseBefore": 0.45
      },
      {
        "text": "One more centimeter, every night.",
        "pauseBefore": 0.4
      },
      {
        "text": "And Theo stopped waking up for the knocks.",
        "pauseBefore": 0.5
      },
      {
        "text": "What knocks? I slept great.",
        "speaker": "theo",
        "pauseBefore": 0.6
      },
      {
        "text": "Then one night, at 3:12, three knocks.",
        "say": "Then one night, at three-twelve, three knocks.",
        "pauseBefore": 0.6
      },
      {
        "text": "Nadia opened Theo's door. His bed was empty.",
        "pauseBefore": 1.8
      },
      {
        "text": "The hallway carpet was pulled tight. Toward the wall.",
        "pauseBefore": 0.55
      },
      {
        "text": "Part four.",
        "pauseBefore": 1.0
      }
    ]
  },
